  "description": "A rule-agnostic MSBuild task that detects references to legacy/forbidden NuGet packages based on consumer-defined LegacyLibraryRule items. This package ships no built-in rules and acts as a lightweight base engine for your own policies. Optionally emits a SARIF report for SonarQube import.",
  "developmentDependency": true,
  "iconFile": "icon.png",
  "id": "LegacyLibAnalyzer",
  "isPrerelease": false,
  "lastEdited": "2026-10-17T19:10:03.463Z",
  "listed": true,
  "packageHash": "k+9Br2Sbub3+CIRAqWIOLMWb26pp9ai1k8WGhYKOYuxHDu9AX6+aGZQO/4OJbTp8Kr2QfrATIe40Demf1oBuNg==",
  "packageHashAlgorithm": "SHA512",
  "packageSize": 83206,
  "published": "2026-10-17T19:06:16.83Z",
  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "0.2.6:\n- Harden the SARIF JSON writer: limit nesting depth, replace lone surrogates, and escape HTML-sensitive and Unicode line separator characters\n0.2.5: package icon\n0.2.4:\n- Ship a net472 task assembly so Visual Studio / msbuild.exe can load the task (MSB4061)- #31\n- Remove dependency on System.Text.Json to avoid runtime conflicts with Visual Studio / msbuild.exe\n0.2.3:\n- Fix MSB4061/MissingMethodException with TaskHostFactory by also packaging LegacyLibAnalyzer.runtimeconfig.json\nalongside the task assembly and its deps.json (the out-of-process task host needs the runtimeconfig.json to resolve the correct runtime/dependencies)\n0.2.2: \n- Fix MSB4061/MissingMethodException with TaskHostFactory by packaging LegacyLibAnalyzer.deps.json alongside the task assembly\n0.2.1: \n- Fix out-of-process execution warning v2\n0.2:\n- Added `Category` option: `Maintainability` (default), `Reliability` or `Security`\n- Renamed `Code` to `ErrorCode`, default to `LegacyLib-Forbidden`\n- Fix out-of-process execution warning\n- .NET 8 support",
